Essentially, the above is correct except for Gehennom and special maze
levels. To make things a bit more complicated, the code has three
different places to decide on trap type: what Janis quoted, predefined
level layout, and the function rndtrap() in sp_lev.c. The latter is
responsible for traps in  maze levels.** This is why you can encounter
fire traps on the Castle level even though they are Gehennom-only.

**Why not special and caverns  levels, even if they go through the
maze loader?

In case you are interested in source diving, the code paths are
outline in http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Trap#References

